@startuml
' Yang Shuo with OpenAI Codex assistance. #641; Zhi Yu's person deletion retained.
' Trace: CanonicalPeopleSession.executeDelete; CanonicalDeleteCommand;
' CanonicalDeleteLessonCommand; PonHubData.removePerson/removeLesson.
!include feature-sequence-style.iuml
participant "session :\nCanonicalPeopleSession" as S
participant "checkCopy :\nPonHubData" as D
participant "executor :\nCanonicalCommandExecutor" as E

alt delete INDEX preview
  S -> S : Resolve current position\nto immutable person record
  S -> D : Test removePerson(id)\non disposable snapshot
  alt referenced by Lesson or attendance
    D --> S : dependency error
  else eligible
    D --> S : check passed
    S -> S : Store pending target;\nreturn confirmation prompt
  end
else delete confirm
  S -> S : Consume pending target
  alt target absent
    note over S : Reject; require a fresh delete INDEX.
  else target present
    S -> E : execute(CanonicalDeleteCommand)
    ref over E : Revalidate staged target;\npersist and publish — Figure 5.2a
  end
else delete cancel
  S -> S : Consume and clear pending target
else deletelesson lid/L1
  S -> E : execute(CanonicalDeleteLessonCommand)
  ref over E : Require empty roster and no attendance;\npersist and publish — Figure 5.2a
end
note over S, E
  Preview and cancellation do not save.
  Every intervening submission clears the target,
  including invalid input (dispatch in Figure 5.1).
  Failed confirmation requires a fresh preview.
  Committed IDs are never reused; no cascading deletion.
end note
@enduml
